  "prefc": "<b>Value</b> here is the city assessor's assessed value, which in Michigan is half of market, so double it for a rough market number. Every lead is absentee by the assessor's own records: no principal residence exemption and the tax bill goes somewhere other than the house. <b>Blight ticket</b> means the city fined the owner for the condition of the building (dangerous, unsafe, vacant and not maintained, bad roof, walls or porch) and the fine went to collections. <b>Registered vacant</b> means the owner told the city the house is empty. <b>Fire damaged</b> means the city is holding part of the owner's fire insurance payout until the house is repaired or torn down.",
